{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/985898-how-to-choose-a-legacy","id":985898,"title":"How to choose a Legacy?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-11T19:48:02-07:00","id":985898,"title":"How to choose a Legacy?","content":"So Ma'ii will need a legacy sooner or later, probably sooner rather than later. As in probably sometime in the next 9xp. (I think I want to get matter to 3 first)<br /> My mage's obsession is in bringing his dead sister back to life.<br /> He is a Moros Arrow, Named after the more sinister coyote of Navajo Mythology.<br /> <br /> How do I pick a Legacy for him? How do you all pick legacies? What should I look for? Or if I make my own, can someone help me?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T23:13:56-07:00","id":985959,"title":"","content":"First - check Path and Order combination. In 2E you <i>can</i> get Legacy from other sources, but it's more difficult. Then look for Arcana Attainments - in RAW of corebook you get Ruling Arcanum of Attainments as Third Ruling to character, but popular is House Rule to get even one from Optional powers if Legacy's Ruling is your Paths Ruling. So check with your ST what is permitted in game. Other than that? Pick something cool and working with your PCs idea. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T07:10:37-07:00","id":986110,"title":"","content":"Thank you <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1437_5.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1437\" data-vbnamecard=\"1437\">wyrdhamster</a> I think that part of my problem is, I look at all the legacies in the 2e book and I ask myself &quot;why would I pick this one?&quot; I feel like walking down My path and among my order there would be tables set up along the way with people from the stone scribes and the bokur waving pamphets and saying &quot;hey come check us out we can help you, what are you studying? What do you want to be? Your studying Prime? Well us Forge Kings are the people to talk to? But why would I pick any one of them over another when I know so little about any of them <br /> <br /> Right now the only one I could go to is the Bokur. My current spread is Death 3 Life 3 Mater 2, and while Bokur are suspected of leaning left handed they aren't (which is fitting) but I'm not sure if they are 100% free council member only, plus I don't know what their attainments are, yantra, oblations, or really anything about them. Plus their reliance on undead servants doesn't fit my image of my character as much. And with a death ruling and mine already being at 3 means...I don't get to enjoy the benefits much<br /> <br /> Otherwise I was thinking of creating a Legacy, if I do that I have longer to wait. But I can make something that is 100% fitting. I still feel like I need some recruiters telling me why I should join their Legacies, and what advantage they will have in working toward my obsession, or in general why I should go to their university.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T07:39:14-07:00","id":986124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HaplessWithDice</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/985898-how-to-choose-a-legacy?p=986110#post986110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Otherwise I was thinking of creating a Legacy, if I do that I have longer to wait. But I can make something that is 100% fitting. I still feel like I need some recruiters telling me why I should join their Legacies, and what advantage they will have in working toward my obsession, or in general why I should go to their university.</div> </div> </div> </div>So let me be your recruiter. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Why to join Legacy?<br /> 1. Third Ruling Arcanum - it really does a lot of charcter custimization. It also nice in universe differe between Path members - one Moros is zombie rising Necromancers, other is Alchemist and next is locking humans souls in urns. ( See Hollow Keepers update I made ).<br /> 2. Attainments - unDissonanceable, spamable spells that works as natural laws of Fallen World. Sweet!<br /> 3. Legacy Oblations - Free Mana each day, without Hallow!<br /> <br /> As to Bokors - if you want to have them in 2E game, start seperate update topic. I gladly help with them. In my signature you have list of Legacies updates made by me to start. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 10-12-2016, 10:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T07:51:48-07:00","id":986132,"title":"","content":"So, there are a lot of legacies and there are a number of them that use Death, Matter or Life in different combinations with each other. It's also possible to join a legacy without knowing the arcana for the Optional attainments and developing that arcana for the optional attainments later.<br /> <br /> You also qualify for Tamers of Rivers both main and optional arcana for instance, they're Matter and Life, a legacy of healers. Think Waterbenders really. That's just one example.<br /> <br /> Whether or not a recruiting table exists kind of depends on the legacy and it's methods of initiation. Some legacies advertise and some make you figure out they exist on your own before considering you. Researching most legacies should be pretty standard library research work for most Mages for surface level info at least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 10-12-2016, 10:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T08:13:15-07:00","id":986143,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/985898-how-to-choose-a-legacy?p=986124#post986124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So let me be your recruiter. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Why to join Legacy?<br /> 1. Third Ruling Arcanum - it really does a lot of charcter custimization. It also nice in universe differe between Path members - one Moros is zombie rising Necromancers, other is Alchemist and next is locking humans souls in urns. ( See Hollow Keepers update I made ).<br /> 2. Attainments - unDissonanceable, spamable spells that works as natural laws of Fallen World. Sweet!<br /> 3. Legacy Oblations - Free Mana each day, without Hallow!<br /> <br /> As to Bokors - if you want to have them in 2E game, start seperate update topic. I gladly help with them. In my signature you have list of Legacies updates made by me to start. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>We can focus on Bokors if that is the right choice for me, which I'm doubting the more I think about it. Some aspects seem fitting others don't. Namely i'm indifferent to the Zombie herd not that they don't seem useful, and might be an attracing element but he hasn't needed to use an ability like that yet.<br /> <br /> Third Ruleing Arcanium, well right now I'd probably be looking at life, or something else? My mage is a dark triskster figure, and one dedicated to the idea of growth through oposition. I rather picture him like Melchior from <a href=\"http://dresdencodak.com/2013/03/19/dark-science-25/\" target=\"_blank\">Dresden Codak</a> and that line &quot;I do not help, I oppose&quot; is something I could see him saying. I understand the reasons to get a legacy (compairing that to a bachelors degree) but from which legacy (school). All of them seem to offer something but I'm not sure which is the right fit for my PC. What infromation would you need to help point me to a few Legacies that might be what I'm looking for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T08:20:10-07:00","id":986148,"title":"","content":"Dark trickster can cover a lot of conceptual ground. Is there a particular trick or approach to conflict resolution? Does he like working with ghosts? Shapeshifting?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T09:19:47-07:00","id":986175,"title":"","content":"I'm of the opinion that you should honestly have a Legacy in mind when you start a character and seed their symbols with ones appropriate for whatever Legacy you want them to join, because otherwise it'll be very difficult when the time comes. Truthfully, as a friend pointed out to me, Legacies are so personal anyway, the idea of Mages joining one rather than all simply founding their own is a bit of a curious feature of the setting.<br /> <br /> <i>That said</i>, it is possible to work backwards; to design a Legacy for your character and then have the ST introduce it as something that already exists; having them stumble upon a mentor or a daimonikon or what have you.<br /> <br /> Also, take a hint from Mrmdubois here too: A Legacy represents a metaphor for how a Mage approaches the Supernal but the Awakened have this habit of making metaphors very literal. Consider a method by which your character resolves issues or how they view something, and then translate that into an action.<br /> <br /> If you wanted to carry on with the Navajo theme, why not have them join the Yee Nahgloshii or the Four Foot Lodge? A Legacy of skinwalkers traditionally considered Left-Handed because so many of their attainments exist to sicken or harm. Perhaps the Four Foot Lodge really is just a bunch of bastard-coated bastards, but perhaps they're also trying to do good; acting as a threat and impediment to those who sin. It's more of a Guardian idea than an Arrow one, but it still works.<br /> <br /> Just making that up off the top of my head, but it's an obvious path to go down.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T09:25:50-07:00","id":986179,"title":"","content":"Upon reading your first post I assumed your character would want to find a way to resurrect his sister by emulating his mythological namesake. My mind went to a trickster Legacy, possibly one that utilizes either Ghosts or laws of the Dead with the goal of confronting an avatar of Death and conning it to get his sister back. Less gloriously, he could raise his sister with an Indefinite Death 5 spell, and patch her up with a stolen Soul, but that doesn't require a Legacy.<br /> <br /> For the record, Legacies in the 2nd Corebook are just a fraction of all written Legacies. If you want a wider selection you can check the thread below. Not only are the Legacies listed, each gets a summary and a commentary. It's reasonable to assume Mages have access to lists just like this one, in-character. You can ask your GM for a session where your character learns of an interesting Legacy and travels abroad to meet its adherents:<br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?658166-Mage-the-Awakening-I-read-a-Legacy-a-day/page49\" target=\"_blank\">I read a Legacy a day</a><br /> <br /> Consider that, even though you choose between a preexisting Legacy and making your own, wiggle room exists. You, as a player, can design a Legacy and your Game-master can make it so that it existed in the setting all along. Not only that, your character can modify an existing Legacy to his liking by developing different Attainments. It can be done in-character, no less. The book doesn't say anything about changing the optional Arcanum to a different one, but nothing should break if you do. Just ask your GM for approval.<br /> <br /> As far as re-skinning goes, consider the following Legacies:<br /> - Katsinam Suukya<br /> - Scions of God<br /> - Keepers of the Covenant<br /> The former two develop themselves after a spiritual patron, and the Coyote is a valid one. All of them interact with Spirits. You could modify any of these to interact with Ghosts and Death-Gods instead. Those are just as an example.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T09:35:07-07:00","id":986183,"title":"","content":"So far, his main trick has been working through ghosts and once using quicken corpse when a horror chased him into a graveyard. Seriously how stupid do you have to be to let the necromancer lead you on a chase into a graveyard? Plus his obsession is resurrecting his sister who has been dead for 8 years.<br /> <br /> Though I have also used shapeshifting once to gain access to an enemy, before assassinating them. Thanks to the fact that their minds didn't register the fact that I was carrying a sword and they mistook me for their lover, so their guard was down.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T11:24:30-07:00","id":986242,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Teatime</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/985898-how-to-choose-a-legacy?p=986179#post986179\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Upon reading your first post I assumed your character would want to find a way to resurrect his sister by emulating his mythological namesake. My mind went to a trickster Legacy, possibly one that utilizes either Ghosts or laws of the Dead with the goal of confronting an avatar of Death and conning it to get his sister back.</div> </div> </div> </div>This, a thousand times this!<br /> <br /> <br /> For the record, Legacies in the 2nd Corebook are just a fraction of all written Legacies. If you want a wider selection you can check the thread below. Not only are the Legacies listed, each gets a summary and a commentary. It's reasonable to assume Mages have access to lists just like this one, in-character. You can ask your GM for a session where your character learns of an interesting Legacy and travels abroad to meet its adherents:<br /> <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">https://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?658166-Mage-the-Awakening-I-read-a-Legacy-a-day/page49&amp;quot;]I</a> read a Legacy a day[/URL]<br /> <br /> Consider that, even though you choose between a preexisting Legacy and making your own, wiggle room exists. You, as a player, can design a Legacy and your Game-master can make it so that it existed in the setting all along. Not only that, your character can modify an existing Legacy to his liking by developing different Attainments. It can be done in-character, no less. The book doesn't say anything about changing the optional Arcanum to a different one, but nothing should break if you do. Just ask your GM for approval.<br /> <br /> As far as re-skinning goes, consider the following Legacies:<br /> - Katsinam Suukya<br /> - Scions of God<br /> - Keepers of the Covenant<br /> The former two develop themselves after a spiritual patron, and the Coyote is a valid one. All of them interact with Spirits. You could modify any of these to interact with Ghosts and Death-Gods instead. Those are just as an example.[/QUOTE]<br /> <br /> I take it death Gods don't interact with the Spirit Arcanium?<br /> <br /> Might do a Scion of Coyote. I'll have to update it, any advice?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T11:32:41-07:00","id":986251,"title":"","content":"Stone Scribes needs to be updated to 2e and would fit the work with ghosts and the dead. Your character could join with the assumption that learning his sister's Final Name can provide strong enough Sympathy to rip her out of the afterlife.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T11:37:15-07:00","id":986257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/985898-how-to-choose-a-legacy?p=986251#post986251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Stone Scribes needs to be updated to 2e and would fit the work with ghosts and the dead. Your character could join with the assumption that learning his sister's Final Name can provide strong enough Sympathy to rip her out of the afterlife.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't I have to be a Mysterium Member for that one?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T11:41:35-07:00","id":986261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/985898-how-to-choose-a-legacy?p=986175#post986175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm of the opinion that you should honestly have a Legacy in mind when you start a character and seed their symbols with ones appropriate for whatever Legacy you want them to join, because otherwise it'll be very difficult when the time comes. Truthfully, as a friend pointed out to me, Legacies are so personal anyway, the idea of Mages joining one rather than all simply founding their own is a bit of a curious feature of the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I agree, building your character with a legacy in mind can be difficult for new players whose only exposure to legacies is the Eleventh Question. And crafting your own seems more like an Advanced Player thing to do but is still the sort of thing that new players can do once they get to that point. Considering how the 'intent' of a created character can differ from the actuality of said character I'd probably suggest holding off even for experienced players.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HaplessWithDice</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/985898-how-to-choose-a-legacy?p=986257#post986257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't I have to be a Mysterium Member for that one?</div> </div> </div> </div>Or Moros. Or Seer of the Throne.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 10-12-2016, 02:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T12:06:07-07:00","id":986289,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/985898-how-to-choose-a-legacy?p=986261#post986261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I agree, building your character with a legacy in mind can be difficult for new players whose only exposure to legacies is the Eleventh Question. And crafting your own seems more like an Advanced Player thing to do but is still the sort of thing that new players can do once they get to that point. Considering how the 'intent' of a created character can differ from the actuality of said character I'd probably suggest holding off even for experienced players.</div> </div> </div> </div>Characters can change in personality, but core symbols rarely do. Still, it's not unreasonable. If you don't like that option, though, the other exists: Create a Legacy for your character and then just have the ST include it in the world somehow for them to join.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T13:23:01-07:00","id":986340,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/985898-how-to-choose-a-legacy?p=986251#post986251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Stone Scribes needs to be updated to 2e and would fit the work with ghosts and the dead. Your character could join with the assumption that learning his sister's Final Name can provide strong enough Sympathy to rip her out of the afterlife.</div> </div> </div> </div>So umm.. how do I do that? I don't even know where the original writeup is.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/985898-how-to-choose-a-legacy?p=986261#post986261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> While I agree, building your character with a legacy in mind can be difficult for new players whose only exposure to legacies is the Eleventh Question. And crafting your own seems more like an Advanced Player thing to do but is still the sort of thing that new players can do once they get to that point. Considering how the 'intent' of a created character can differ from the actuality of said character I'd probably suggest holding off even for experienced players.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that is why I'd rather modify an existing one to fit my needs, but also making my own based on strait up being a force of opposition seems amusing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/985898-how-to-choose-a-legacy?p=986261#post986261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Or Moros. Or Seer of the Throne.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ohh okay I'm already a Moros so I'm good then.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/985898-how-to-choose-a-legacy?p=986289#post986289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Characters can change in personality, but core symbols rarely do. Still, it's not unreasonable. If you don't like that option, though, the other exists: Create a Legacy for your character and then just have the ST include it in the world somehow for them to join.</div> </div> </div> </div>Someone suggested modifying something like Scions of God to be more like Scions of Coyote, and modifying it be reflect a different arcanum, and doing things like tricking a death god and getting my sister back from the here after that way, suggesting it would that be easier than making my own, and I could see variations of legacies being a thing too.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T13:33:31-07:00","id":986349,"title":"","content":"Stone Scribes are in Legcaies the Sublime. It's supposedly Fate and Death, but honestly I think you could pull their tricks off with just Death easily enough. I'd probably want to pair it with Time to more easily plumb the past for more Final Names, but it doesn't have to be that way.<br /> <br /> Scribes can also be found in the Arrow and FC by the way. Apparently they get around a bit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T15:00:26-07:00","id":986411,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HaplessWithDice</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/985898-how-to-choose-a-legacy?p=986242#post986242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I take it death Gods don't interact with the Spirit Arcanium?</div> </div> </div> </div>When I said &quot;Death-Gods&quot; I meant Kerberoi, Chthonians and Deathlords - all inhabitants of the Underworld. Many of these will be of Rank 6+, so they won't be pushed around by basic Death magic. However, Ghosts and lesser Chthonians will be, and will serve as necessary training for the character. The problem is that ultimately it's the Deathlords Ma'ii needs to negotiate with, but they have never been written up.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HaplessWithDice</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/985898-how-to-choose-a-legacy?p=986242#post986242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Might do a Scion of Coyote. I'll have to update it, any advice?</div> </div> </div> </div>Scions of God have Attainments chiefly for Spirit and Shadow interaction. Given your character's goal, finding analogues in the Death Arcanum is an obvious approach. One of their later Attainments gives them an alternate form while in Twilight, but it can be merely an aesthetic change. I think it could be lifted to give Ma'ii a Coyote-like form in Twilight and the Underworld. The Coyote worship doesn't have to be an intrinsic part of the Legacy either. Ma'ii might just engage in both. I also believe Fate is very fitting for what you're going for, since it covers contracts, general trickery and can circumvent Old Laws of the Underworld. The thing to consider is which Arcanum to make Legacy Ruling. If it's Death, your character can enter the Legacy very soon. If it's Fate (or anything else) you get an extra Ruling Arcanum, but must spend much more XP before joining.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T14:23:26-07:00","id":986951,"title":"","content":"Okay so I have 3 Legacies I am working on <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/17jZ0Jg-fvoyW1MIy79ZswT8a56-5-fbJnj17DhdFA1A/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Scions of Death</a>, Stone Scribes, and White Reaper (A combat oriented Legacy I thought up over lunch, yes it is Left Handed trying to be less Left handed).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T15:33:43-07:00","id":986980,"title":"","content":"There are a LOT of Legacies, spread out over the 1st Edition books. If you're still looking for ideas, this may help in identifying and tracking the ones down you might be interested in:<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://wodcodex.com/wiki/Legacies_(1st_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://wodcodex.com/wiki/Legacies_(1st_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\"> 404 Not Found </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://wodcodex.com/wiki/Legacies_(1st_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\"> http://wodcodex.com/wiki/Legacies_(1st_Edition) </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11818-romzombie","name":"ROMzombie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T05:21:40-07:00","id":987202,"title":"","content":"Thanks <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11818-romzombie\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11818_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11818\" data-vbnamecard=\"11818\">ROMzombie</a>, I think I narrowed it down the only problem is a lot of those haven't been updated to 2e yet. I'm trying to warp one, write one, and update one on my own right now. The warp one is tough enough, because I'm trying to follow the outline of the 1e attainment just mold it to death. Trying to update stone scribe is going to be tough too, and I might talk to <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1437_5.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1437\" data-vbnamecard=\"1437\">wyrdhamster</a> about it if. Maybe see if they can be encouraged to maybe prioritize that one on their blog to update it sooner. Otherwise I said I'd try it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http:/